diff --git a/debian/patches/0903-add-dolby-vision-rpu-passthrough-to-hevc-nvenc-encoder.patch b/debian/patches/0903-add-dolby-vision-rpu-passthrough-to-hevc-nvenc-encoder.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/debian/patches/0903-add-dolby-vision-rpu-passthrough-to-hevc-nvenc-encoder.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,1114 @@
+Add Dolby Vision RPU passthrough to the HEVC NVENC encoder.
+
+hevc_nvenc drops Dolby Vision on transcode, the same way hevc_vaapi did before
+0004: only libx265, libsvtav1 and libaomenc call ff_dovi_configure(). This
+wires hevc_nvenc to the existing DOVI code and moves the profile 8.1
+conversion that 0004 grew into a shared file so both encoders run one copy.
+
+Four things about the mechanism are not obvious.
+
+1. The RPU is a SUFFIX NAL (type 62, UNSPEC62), so unlike the A53 and timecode
+   payloads it cannot go through NVENC's seiPayloadArray -- that writes SEI NAL
+   types only. It is appended to the coded packet in process_output_surface()
+   instead, which is what dovi_tool's inject-rpu and rigaya's NVEncC both do.
+
+2. With B-frames the encoder emits pictures out of display order, so the RPU
+   has to travel with its picture rather than with the submission sequence.
+   Nothing new is needed for that: nvenc_store_frame_data() already writes a
+   per-frame slot and smuggles the index out through pic_params->inputDuration,
+   and NVENC hands the same value back as lock_params->outputDuration. The RPU
+   becomes a third field in that slot, alongside duration and frame_opaque.
+   Note the slot index wraps modulo frame_data_array_nb, so it is NOT the frame
+   number -- do not use it as one.
+
+   process_output_surface() peeks at the slot rather than consuming it, because
+   the packet has to be sized for bitstreamSizeInBytes + the RPU before
+   ff_get_encode_buffer() allocates it. nvenc_retrieve_frame_data() still owns
+   freeing it.
+
+3. ff_dovi_configure() reads avctx->pix_fmt, which for a hardware chain is
+   AV_PIX_FMT_CUDA or AV_PIX_FMT_D3D11 and says nothing about the coded
+   samples, so the profile check would reject every stream. Pass the coded
+   format explicitly via ff_dovi_configure_from_codedpar() instead, using
+   ctx->data_pix_fmt, which nvenc has already resolved. This is the same
+   workaround 0004 needs and for the same reason.
+
+4. -dolbyvision defaults to 'auto', which engages only when
+   avctx->decoded_side_data carries an AVDOVIMetadata. The ffmpeg CLI never
+   populates it, so the default drops Dolby Vision entirely -- libx265 behaves
+   identically. -dolbyvision 1 is required in practice, and a frame arriving
+   with DV metadata while no profile is active warns once.
+
+   That warning is gated on AV_CODEC_ID_HEVC. ff_nvenc_encode_init() is shared
+   by every nvenc encoder, but only hevc_nvenc declares -dolbyvision, and
+   telling an h264 or av1 user to pass an option their encoder does not have
+   would be worse than saying nothing.
+
+The shared file, libavcodec/dovi_p81.{c,h}, carries the profile 4/7 -> 8.1
+conversion, the FEL/MEL discrimination, the L5 handling and the option
+declarations. Two things there are structural rather than conventional:
+FF_DOVI_P81_L5_OPTIONS() means both encoders cannot spell the options
+differently, and ff_dovi_p81_check_options() means neither can forget that
+dv_l5=scale without dv_l5_canvas is a division by zero rather than a
+diagnostic. 0004's own copy of that code is removed here, so this patch must
+apply after it.
+
+Verified on an RTX A4000 (driver 595.71.05), against a shared build of the
+same source:
+
+  P8 bl1 (8.1)            profile 8 / compat 1 tag, 20/20 frames carry an RPU
+  P7 FEL                  converted; header and rpu_data_mapping byte-identical
+                          to dovi_tool -m 2 on the same window
+  P7 MEL                  converted, byte-identical to dovi_tool -m 2 as well;
+                          logged as MEL, and the FEL-only mapping reset does not
+                          fire -- only the NLQ fields change
+  P5                      NOT converted; profile 5 / compat 0 in and out
+  P8 bl6                  passes through, compat id derived to 1
+  dual-track P7           fails cleanly, exit 183, "received frame without
+                          AV_FRAME_DATA_DOVI_METADATA"
+  B-frames (-bf 3)        71 B / 1 I / 24 P, and across 96 frames every packet
+                          fetched the slot its own frame was stored in, 0
+                          exceptions. The one distinctively sized RPU landed on
+                          the frame where the source's L1 scene change is.
+  pixels                  framemd5-IDENTICAL with DV on vs off, 48/48 frames
+  rate control            RPU byte-identical between constqp and VBR
+  mp4                     dvcC written with -strict unofficial, absent without
+  auto                    warns once, produces no DV
+
+That covers every Dolby Vision shape in the library this was built for.
+
+Not covered: the MEL branch is proven to be TAKEN, not to preserve a mapping --
+the MEL source available also carries the identity mapping, so reset and
+no-reset emit the same bytes on it. Profile 4 has no content to test against.
+No Windows encode was run, but there is no Windows-specific code here to get
+wrong: both AV_PIX_FMT_CUDA and AV_PIX_FMT_D3D11 collapse into
+ctx->data_pix_fmt on one shared line at the top of ff_nvenc_encode_init(),
+before any of this runs, and the DV code names neither. The side data comes
+from ff_dovi_attach_side_data() in the HEVC decoder's output path, which is not
+gated on hwaccel. Untested only as an end-to-end formality. av1_nvenc is untouched -- AV1 Dolby Vision is profile 10, which needs
+the T.35 metadata OBU path.
+
